<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Case File — Operational Efficiency Internship Report</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..144,400;0,9..144,600;0,9..144,700;1,9..144,500&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  :root{
    --teal-950:#0d2b2c;
    --teal-900:#123338;
    --teal-800:#194045;
    --paper:#f3eee1;
    --paper-2:#eae2cd;
    --line:#cdc0a0;
    --ink:#211d16;
    --ink-soft:#57503f;
    --rust:#a8432f;
    --rust-dark:#822f20;
    --gold:#b98a34;
    --gold-soft:#e4c581;
    --ok:#3d6b4c;
    --shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(13,43,44,0.18);
    --radius: 3px;
    --font-display: 'Fraunces', serif;
    --font-body: 'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif;
    --font-mono: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
  }

  *{box-sizing:border-box;}
  html,body{margin:0;padding:0;}
  body{
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    color: var(--ink);
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse at top left, rgba(185,138,52,0.06), transparent 45%),
      var(--paper);
    background-attachment: fixed;
    min-height:100vh;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }

  body::before{
    content:"";
    position:fixed; inset:0;
    background-image:
      repeating-linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(33,29,22,0.015) 0px, rgba(33,29,22,0.015) 1px, transparent 1px, transparent 3px);
    pointer-events:none;
    z-index:0;
  }

  h1,h2,h3,h4{ font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight:600; margin:0; color:var(--teal-950); }
  p{ line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 12px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  a{ color: var(--rust); }
  button{ font-family: var(--font-body); cursor:pointer; }
  ::selection{ background: var(--gold-soft); }

  :focus-visible{
    outline: 2px solid var(--rust);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce){
    *{ animation-duration: 0.001ms !important; transition-duration: 0.001ms !important; }
  }

  .hidden{ display:none !important; }

  .eyebrow{
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--rust);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* ===== STAMP ===== */
  .stamp{
    position:relative;
    display:inline-flex;
    align-items:center;
    gap:8px;
    border:2px solid var(--rust);
    color:var(--rust);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size:11px;
    letter-spacing:0.12em;
    text-transform:uppercase;
    padding:6px 12px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    transform: rotate(-3deg);
    opacity:0.85;
  }
  .stamp::before{ content:"●"; font-size:8px; }

  /* ===== GATE / LOGIN SCREENS ===== */
  .screen{
    position:relative;
    z-index:1;
    min-height:100vh;
    width:100%;
  }

  .center-wrap{
    min-height:100vh;
    display:flex;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding: 32px 20px;
  }

  .dossier{
    width:100%;
    max-width: 860px;
    background: var(--teal-900);
    color: #efe8d3;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    overflow:hidden;
    position:relative;
  }
  .dossier::after{
    content:"";
    position:absolute; left:0; top:0; bottom:0; width:54px;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(180deg, var(--rust) 0 26px, transparent 26px 52px);
    opacity:0.15;
  }

  .dossier-inner{ padding: 48px 52px 44px; position:relative; }
  @media (max-width:640px){ .dossier-inner{ padding: 34px 24px 30px; } }

  .dossier .eyebrow{ color: var(--gold-soft); }
  .dossier h1{
    color:#fbf7ea;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 40px);
    margin: 10px 0 6px;
    line-height:1.1;
  }
  .dossier .sub{ color:#c9d6d2; font-size:15px; max-width:520px; margin-bottom:28px; }

  .gate-choices{ display:grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap:16px; margin-top: 20px; }
  @media (max-width:640px){ .gate-choices{ grid-template-columns:1fr; } }

  .choice-card{
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04);
    border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.14);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding:22px 20px;
    text-align:left;
    color:#efe8d3;
    transition: border-color .15s ease, background .15s ease, transform .15s ease;
  }
  .choice-card:hover{ border-color: var(--gold); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.07); transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .choice-card .tag{ font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:10px; letter-spacing:0.12em; text-transform:uppercase; color: var(--gold-soft); }
  .choice-card h3{ color:#fbf7ea; margin:8px 0 6px; font-size:19px; }
  .choice-card span.desc{ display:block; font-size:13px; color:#b9c4bf; line-height:1.5; }

  .form-stack{ display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:14px; margin-top:22px; max-width:420px; }
  .field label{ display:block; font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:11px; letter-spacing:0.08em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--gold-soft); margin-bottom:6px; }
  .field input{
    width:100%; padding:12px 14px; border-radius:2px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.22);
    background: rgba(0,0,0,0.18); color:#fbf7ea; font-family:var(--font-body); font-size:14px;
  }
  .field input::placeholder{ color:#7f8f8a; }
  .field input:focus{ border-color: var(--gold); }

  .btn{
    display:inline-flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; gap:8px;
    padding: 13px 22px; border-radius:2px; border:none; font-weight:600; font-size:14px;
    letter-spacing:0.02em; transition: filter .15s ease, transform .1s ease;
  }
  .btn:active{ transform: translateY(1px); }
  .btn-primary{ background: var(--rust); color:#fbf1e8; }
  .btn-primary:hover{ filter:brightness(1.08); }
  .btn-ghost{ background: transparent; color:#efe8d3; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.3); }
  .btn-ghost:hover{ border-color:#fbf7ea; }
  .btn-gold{ background: var(--gold); color:#241a05; }
  .btn-gold:hover{ filter:brightness(1.06); }
  .btn-danger{ background: transparent; border:1px solid var(--rust); color:var(--rust); }
  .btn-danger:hover{ background: var(--rust); color:#fff; }
  .btn-sm{ padding:8px 14px; font-size:12.5px; }
  .btn:disabled{ opacity:0.45; cursor:not-allowed; }

  .back-link{ background:none; border:none; color:#b9c4bf; font-size:12.5px; margin-top:18px; text-decoration:underline; padding:0; }

  .error-msg{ color: #ffb199; font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:12px; min-height:16px; }

  /* ===== DASHBOARD SHELL ===== */
  .topbar{
    position:sticky; top:0; z-index:20;
    background: var(--teal-950);
    color:#efe8d3;
    padding: 14px 26px;
    display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; gap:16px;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 18px rgba(0,0,0,0.18);
  }
  .topbar .brand{ display:flex; align-items:center; gap:12px; }
  .topbar .brand .mark{ width:34px; height:34px; border:2px solid var(--gold); border-radius:50%; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-family:var(--font-display); font-weight:700; color:var(--gold); font-size:15px;}
  .topbar .brand-text .name{ font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:16px; color:#fbf7ea; line-height:1.1; }
  .topbar .brand-text .role{ font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:10px; letter-spacing:0.1em; color:#9db3ac; text-transform:uppercase; }
  .topbar .who{ display:flex; align-items:center; gap:14px; }
  .topbar .who .who-name{ font-size:13px; color:#d9d2bb; }
  .topbar .who .who-name b{ color:#fbf7ea; }

  .tabs{
    display:flex; gap:4px; overflow-x:auto; padding: 0 20px; background: var(--teal-900);
    border-bottom: 3px solid var(--gold);
  }
  .tab-btn{
    background: var(--teal-800); color:#c9d6d2; border:none; padding:12px 18px;
    font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:11.5px; letter-spacing:0.06em; text-transform:uppercase;
    border-radius: 6px 6px 0 0; white-space:nowrap; margin-top:6px; opacity:0.75;
  }
  .tab-btn.active{ background: var(--paper); color:var(--teal-950); opacity:1; font-weight:600; }

  .content-wrap{ max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 30px 24px 90px; position:relative; z-index:1; }

  .panel{ display:none; animation: fadein .25s ease; }
  .panel.active{ display:block; }
  @keyframes fadein{ from{opacity:0; transform:translateY(6px);} to{opacity:1; transform:translateY(0);} }

  .section-head{ margin-bottom:22px; }
  .section-head h2{ font-size: clamp(22px,3vw,30px); margin-top:4px; }
  .section-head .desc{ max-width:640px; margin-top:8px; }

  .card{
    background:#fffdf7;
    border:1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    box-shadow: 0 2px 0 var(--line);
  }

  .grid-2{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:20px; }
  .grid-3{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); gap:18px; }
  @media (max-width:900px){ .grid-2, .grid-3{ grid-template-columns:1fr; } }

  /* stat / index cards */
  .index-card{
    background:#fffdf7; border:1px solid var(--line); border-left:4px solid var(--rust);
    padding:18px 20px; border-radius:var(--radius);
  }
  .index-card .num{ font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:32px; color:var(--teal-950); line-height:1; }
  .index-card .label{ font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:11px; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.06em; color:var(--ink-soft); margin-top:8px; display:block; }

  .banner{
    background: var(--teal-900); color:#efe8d3; padding:18px 22px; border-radius:var(--radius);
    margin-bottom: 26px; display:flex; align-items:center; gap:14px; border-left:5px solid var(--gold);
  }
  .banner .banner-text{ font-size:14px; line-height:1.5; }
  .banner .banner-text b{ color:#fbf7ea; }

  /* folder tab card wrapper for content blocks */
  .folder{
    position:relative; margin-top: 34px;
  }
  .folder-tab{
    display:inline-block; background: var(--teal-900); color:var(--gold-soft);
    font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:11px; letter-spacing:0.08em; text-transform:uppercase;
    padding:6px 16px; border-radius:4px 4px 0 0; position:relative; top:1px;
  }
  .folder-body{
    background:#fffdf7; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:0 6px 6px 6px; padding: 24px;
  }

  .timeline{ position:relative; margin-top: 10px; padding-left: 26px; border-left:2px dashed var(--line); }
  .tl-item{ position:relative; padding-bottom: 26px; }
  .tl-item:last-child{ padding-bottom:0; }
  .tl-item::before{
    content:""; position:absolute; left:-33px; top:2px; width:14px; height:14px; border-radius:50%;
    background: var(--paper); border:3px solid var(--rust);
  }
  .tl-item h4{ font-size:15.5px; color:var(--teal-950); }
  .tl-item .tl-tag{ font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:10px; color:var(--rust); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.08em; }
  .tl-item p{ margin-top:6px; font-size:13.5px; }

  .quote-block{
    background: var(--paper-2); border:1px solid var(--line); border-left:5px solid var(--gold);
    padding:22px 24px; border-radius:var(--radius); font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style:italic; font-size:16px; color:var(--teal-950); line-height:1.55; position:relative;
  }
  .quote-block cite{ display:block; margin-top:12px; font-family:var(--font-mono); font-style:normal; font-size:11px; color:var(--ink-soft); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.04em; }

  .chart-card{ background:#fffdf7; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:var(--radius); padding:20px; }
  .chart-card h3{ font-size:16px; margin-bottom:4px; }
  .chart-card .note{ font-size:12px; color:var(--ink-soft); margin-bottom:14px; }
  .chart-holder{ position:relative; }
  .chart-holder.scrolls{ overflow-x:auto; padding-bottom:6px; }
  .svg-chart{ width:100%; }
  .svg-chart svg{ display:block; }
  .chart-legend{ display:flex; gap:18px; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-bottom:14px; }
  .chart-legend .leg-item{ display:flex; align-items:center; gap:7px; font-size:12px; color:var(--ink-soft); font-family:var(--font-mono); }
  .chart-legend .leg-swatch{ width:12px; height:12px; border-radius:3px; display:inline-block; }

  .findings-list{ list-style:none; margin:0; padding:0; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:10px; }
  .findings-list li{
    display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:flex-start; font-size:13.5px; color:var(--ink); background:#fffdf7;
    border:1px solid var(--line); padding:10px 14px; border-radius:var(--radius);
  }
  .findings-list li .n{ font-family:var(--font-mono); color:var(--rust); font-weight:600; flex:none; }

  .flow{
    display:flex; align-items:center; gap:10px; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-top:18px;
  }
  .flow .fbox{
    background: var(--teal-900); color:#efe8d3; padding:14px 16px; border-radius:6px; font-size:12.5px;
    max-width:190px; line-height:1.45; border:1px solid var(--teal-800);
  }
  .flow .fbox b{ display:block; color:#fbf7ea; font-size:12.5px; margin-bottom:4px; font-family:var(--font-mono); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.04em;}
  .flow .arrow{ color:var(--rust); font-size:20px; }
  .flow .fbox.branch-yes{ border-color: var(--ok); }
  .flow .fbox.branch-no{ border-color: var(--rust); }

  .incentive-grid{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); gap:16px; margin-top:18px; }
  @media (max-width:960px){ .incentive-grid{ grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; } }
  @media (max-width:640px){ .incentive-grid{ grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
  .incentive-card{
    background:#fffdf7; border:1px solid var(--line); border-top:4px solid var(--gold); border-radius:var(--radius);
    padding:16px 16px 18px;
  }
  .incentive-card h4{ font-size:14.5px; margin-bottom:8px; color:var(--teal-950); }
  .incentive-card p{ font-size:12.5px; margin:0; }

  .team-strip{
    display:flex; gap:14px; align-items:center; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-top:8px;
  }
  .avatar-chip{
    display:flex; align-items:center; gap:10px; background:#fffdf7; border:1px solid var(--line);
    padding:8px 14px 8px 8px; border-radius:30px; font-size:13px;
  }
  .avatar-chip .dot{ width:30px; height:30px; border-radius:50%; background:var(--teal-900); color:#fbf7ea; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:13px; }

  .download-panel{
    background: var(--teal-900); border-radius:var(--radius); padding: 30px; color:#efe8d3;
    display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; gap:24px; flex-wrap:wrap;
  }
  .download-panel h3{ color:#fbf7ea; font-size:20px; margin-bottom:6px; }
  .download-panel p{ color:#c9d6d2; font-size:13.5px; max-width:440px; margin:0; }

  /* feedback modal */
  .modal-overlay{
    position:fixed; inset:0; background: rgba(13,43,44,0.7); z-index:100; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; padding:20px;
  }
  .modal-box{
    background: var(--paper); border-radius:var(--radius); max-width:460px; width:100%; padding: 30px 28px; box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .modal-box h3{ font-size:20px; margin-bottom:6px; }
  .modal-box p.hint{ font-size:13px; color:var(--ink-soft); margin-bottom:18px; }
  .star-row{ display:flex; gap:8px; margin-bottom:18px; }
  .star-btn{ background:none; border:none; font-size:28px; color:var(--line); padding:0; line-height:1; }
  .star-btn.filled{ color:var(--gold); }
  .modal-box textarea{
    width:100%; min-height:90px; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:2px; padding:10px 12px;
    font-family:var(--font-body); font-size:13.5px; resize:vertical; background:#fffdf7;
  }
  .modal-actions{ display:flex; justify-content:flex-end; gap:10px; margin-top:18px; }

  /* admin */
  .admin-grid{ display:grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap:16px; }
  table.data-table{ width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; font-size:13px; background:#fffdf7; }
  table.data-table th{
    text-align:left; font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:10.5px; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.05em;
    color:var(--ink-soft); border-bottom:2px solid var(--teal-900); padding:9px 10px; background:var(--paper-2);
  }
  table.data-table td{ padding:10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); vertical-align:top; }
  table.data-table tr:hover td{ background: rgba(185,138,52,0.06); }
  .stars-static{ color:var(--gold); letter-spacing:1px; font-size:13px; }
  .empty-state{ padding:40px 20px; text-align:center; color:var(--ink-soft); font-size:13.5px; }
  .empty-state .big{ font-size:34px; display:block; margin-bottom:8px; }

  .editor-field{ margin-bottom:18px; }
  .editor-field label{ display:block; font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:11px; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.06em; color:var(--ink-soft); margin-bottom:6px; }
  .editor-field textarea, .editor-field input{
    width:100%; padding:10px 12px; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:2px; font-family:var(--font-body); font-size:13.5px; background:#fffdf7;
  }
  .editor-field textarea{ min-height:80px; resize:vertical; }
  .save-row{ display:flex; align-items:center; gap:12px; }
  .save-msg{ font-size:12.5px; color: var(--ok); font-family:var(--font-mono); opacity:0; transition:opacity .3s ease; }
  .save-msg.show{ opacity:1; }

  .editor-group{ background:#fffdf7; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:var(--radius); margin-bottom:14px; overflow:hidden; }
  .editor-group summary{
    cursor:pointer; padding:14px 18px; font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:12px; text-transform:uppercase;
    letter-spacing:0.06em; color:var(--teal-950); background: var(--paper-2); font-weight:600; list-style:none;
    display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between;
  }
  .editor-group summary::-webkit-details-marker{ display:none; }
  .editor-group summary::after{ content:'+'; font-size:16px; color:var(--rust); }
  .editor-group[open] summary::after{ content:'–'; }
  .editor-group .editor-group-body{ padding:18px; }

  .toast{
    position:fixed; bottom:24px; left:50%; transform:translateX(-50%); background:var(--teal-950); color:#fbf7ea;
    padding:12px 20px; border-radius:4px; font-size:13px; z-index:200; box-shadow:var(--shadow); border-left:4px solid var(--gold);
  }

  .badge-count{ background:var(--rust); color:#fff; font-size:10px; padding:2px 7px; border-radius:20px; margin-left:6px; font-family:var(--font-mono); }

  footer.sign{ text-align:center; padding: 26px; font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:11px; color:var(--ink-soft); }

  /* ===== INTERACTIVE PAGE FRAME ===== */
  .page-frame{ position:fixed; inset:0; pointer-events:none; z-index:9999; }
  .page-frame .edge{ position:absolute; opacity:0.6; }
  .page-frame .edge.top, .page-frame .edge.bottom{
    left:0; right:0; height:4px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--rust) 20%, var(--gold) 50%, var(--rust) 80%, transparent);
    background-size: 260% 100%;
    animation: frameShimmerH 10s linear infinite;
  }
  .page-frame .edge.top{ top:0; }
  .page-frame .edge.bottom{ bottom:0; animation-direction:reverse; }
  .page-frame .edge.left, .page-frame .edge.right{
    top:0; bottom:0; width:4px;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, transparent, var(--gold) 20%, var(--rust) 50%, var(--gold) 80%, transparent);
    background-size: 100% 260%;
    animation: frameShimmerV 12s linear infinite;
  }
  .page-frame .edge.left{ left:0; }
  .page-frame .edge.right{ right:0; animation-direction:reverse; }
  @keyframes frameShimmerH{ from{ background-position:0% 0; } to{ background-position:260% 0; } }
  @keyframes frameShimmerV{ from{ background-position:0 0%; } to{ background-position:0 260%; } }

  .page-frame .corner{ position:absolute; width:30px; height:30px; transition: border-color .2s ease, width .2s ease, height .2s ease; }
  .page-frame .corner.tl{ top:10px; left:10px; border-top:3px solid var(--gold); border-left:3px solid var(--gold); }
  .page-frame .corner.tr{ top:10px; right:10px; border-top:3px solid var(--gold); border-right:3px solid var(--gold); }
  .page-frame .corner.bl{ bottom:10px; left:10px; border-bottom:3px solid var(--gold); border-left:3px solid var(--gold); }
  .page-frame .corner.br{ bottom:10px; right:10px; border-bottom:3px solid var(--gold); border-right:3px solid var(--gold); }
  body.frame-active .page-frame .corner{ border-color: var(--rust); width:38px; height:38px; }

  .page-frame .glow{
    position:absolute; width:280px; height:280px; border-radius:50%;
    background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(185,138,52,0.32), transparent 70%);
    left: calc(var(--spot-x, 50%) - 140px); top: calc(var(--spot-y, 50%) - 140px);
    filter: blur(4px); opacity:0; transition: opacity .25s ease;
  }
  body.frame-active .page-frame .glow{ opacity:1; }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce){
    .page-frame .edge{ animation:none; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page-frame" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="edge top"></div>
  <div class="edge bottom"></div>
  <div class="edge left"></div>
  <div class="edge right"></div>
  <div class="corner tl"></div>
  <div class="corner tr"></div>
  <div class="corner bl"></div>
  <div class="corner br"></div>
  <div class="glow"></div>
</div>

<div id="app">

  <!-- ===================== GATE ===================== -->
  <section id="view-gate" class="screen">
    <div class="center-wrap">
      <div class="dossier">
        <div class="dossier-inner">
          <span class="stamp">Confidential · Internship Case File</span>
          <h1>Increasing Operational Efficiency<br>in Customer Service</h1>
          <p class="sub">Final internship deliverable — a working record of the Bengaluru facility deep-dive, the Pan-India operations survey, and the Astra adoption findings gathered over the placement period.</p>
          <div class="gate-choices">
            <button class="choice-card" id="btn-go-user">
              <span class="tag">Enter Dashboard</span>
              <h3>Viewer Access →</h3>
              <span class="desc">Sign the visitor log with your name and email to open the interactive case file.</span>
            </button>
            <button class="choice-card" id="btn-go-admin">
              <span class="tag">Restricted</span>
              <h3>Admin Access →</h3>
              <span class="desc">Review the visitor log, read feedback, and edit dashboard content.</span>
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== USER LOGIN ===================== -->
  <section id="view-user-login" class="screen hidden">
    <div class="center-wrap">
      <div class="dossier">
        <div class="dossier-inner">
          <span class="eyebrow">Visitor Log · Entry Required</span>
          <h1 style="font-size:28px; margin-top:10px;">Sign in to open the case file</h1>
          <p class="sub">Your name and email are recorded so the report owner knows who reviewed it. Nothing else is required.</p>
          <form id="user-login-form" class="form-stack">
            <div class="field">
              <label for="u-name">Full name</label>
              <input type="text" id="u-name" placeholder="e.g. Priya Sharma" required autocomplete="name">
            </div>
            <div class="field">
              <label for="u-email">Email address</label>
              <input type="email" id="u-email" placeholder="you@company.com" required autocomplete="email">
            </div>
            <div class="error-msg" id="u-login-error"></div>
            <div style="display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:center; margin-top:6px;">
              <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Open Case File</button>
              <button type="button" class="back-link" data-back="view-gate">← back</button>
            </div>
          </form>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== ADMIN LOGIN ===================== -->
  <section id="view-admin-login" class="screen hidden">
    <div class="center-wrap">
      <div class="dossier">
        <div class="dossier-inner">
          <span class="eyebrow">Restricted Area</span>
          <h1 style="font-size:28px; margin-top:10px;">Admin sign-in</h1>
          <p class="sub">Only the report owner should have these credentials.</p>
          <form id="admin-login-form" class="form-stack">
            <div class="field">
              <label for="a-user">User ID</label>
              <input type="text" id="a-user" placeholder="User ID" required autocomplete="username">
            </div>
            <div class="field">
              <label for="a-pass">Password</label>
              <input type="password" id="a-pass" placeholder="Password" required autocomplete="current-password">
            </div>
            <div class="error-msg" id="a-login-error"></div>
            <div style="display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:center; margin-top:6px;">
              <button type="submit" class="btn btn-gold">Unlock Admin View</button>
              <button type="button" class="back-link" data-back="view-gate">← back</button>
            </div>
          </form>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== PROJECT OVERVIEW / SELECTOR ===================== -->
  <section id="view-overview" class="screen hidden">
    <div class="center-wrap">
      <div class="dossier" style="max-width:980px;">
        <div class="dossier-inner">
          <span class="eyebrow">Program Overview</span>
          <h1 style="font-size:clamp(26px,3.6vw,36px);">Everything comes back to the customer</h1>
          <p class="sub" style="max-width:640px;">Welcome.</p>

          <div class="incentive-grid" style="margin-top:8px;">
            <div class="incentive-card" style="border-top-color:var(--gold-soft); background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04); border-color:rgba(255,255,255,0.14);">
              <h4 style="color:#fbf7ea;">Improve customer experience</h4>
              <p style="color:#c9d6d2;">Make the everyday interaction — pickup, retrieval, status, response — easier for the person on the other end.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="incentive-card" style="border-top-color:var(--gold-soft); background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04); border-color:rgba(255,255,255,0.14);">
              <h4 style="color:#fbf7ea;">Increase revenue</h4>
              <p style="color:#c9d6d2;">Find where existing tools and relationships are under-monetised, and where new services can be sold in.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="incentive-card" style="border-top-color:var(--gold-soft); background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04); border-color:rgba(255,255,255,0.14);">
              <h4 style="color:#fbf7ea;">Decrease cost</h4>
              <p style="color:#c9d6d2;">Cut the manual, repetitive, status-chasing work that quietly eats staff time across branches.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="incentive-card" style="border-top-color:var(--gold-soft); background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04); border-color:rgba(255,255,255,0.14);">
              <h4 style="color:#fbf7ea;">Improve customer relationship</h4>
              <p style="color:#c9d6d2;">Move from being a vendor prospects tolerate to a partner they actively want to expand with.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p class="sub" style="margin-top:26px; margin-bottom:6px;">Two placement projects, two different levers on the same goal:</p>
          <div class="gate-choices">
            <button class="choice-card" id="btn-select-p1">
              <span class="tag">Project One · Revenue &amp; Cost</span>
              <h3>Operational Efficiency →</h3>
              <span class="desc">A two-phase investigation into customer-service operations — the Bengaluru facility walkthrough and the Pan-India survey — aimed at cutting cost and unlocking revenue by fixing how requests actually move.</span>
            </button>
            <button class="choice-card" id="btn-select-p2">
              <span class="tag">Project Two · Customer Relationship</span>
              <h3>Enterprise Prospect Strategy →</h3>
              <span class="desc">A data-driven analysis of 38 enterprise prospects — PESTEL, compliance, digital maturity, financials — to grow revenue by deepening the customer relationship, not just adding a tool.</span>
            </button>
          </div>

          <div style="margin-top:24px;">
            <button type="button" class="back-link" id="btn-overview-logout">← log out</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== USER DASHBOARD ===================== -->
  <section id="view-dashboard" class="screen hidden">
    <div class="topbar">
      <div class="brand">
        <div class="mark">CR</div>
        <div class="brand-text">
          <div class="name">Project One · Operational Efficiency</div>
          <div class="role">Revenue &amp; Cost · Internship Project</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="who">
        <button class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" id="btn-projects-p1">← All Projects</button>
        <span class="who-name">Signed in as <b id="dash-who-name">—</b></span>
        <button class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" id="btn-logout">Log out</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tabs" id="user-tabs">
      <button class="tab-btn active" data-panel="p-phase1">Phase 1 · Bengaluru</button>
      <button class="tab-btn" data-panel="p-phase2">Phase 2 · Pan-India</button>
      <button class="tab-btn" data-panel="p-astra">Findings</button>
      <button class="tab-btn" data-panel="p-incentive">Incentive Plan</button>
      <button class="tab-btn" data-panel="p-roadmap">Automation Roadmap</button>
      <button class="tab-btn" data-panel="p-report">Download Report</button>
    </div>

    <div class="content-wrap">
      <div class="banner">
        <div class="banner-text"><b>Note:</b> <span data-ck="overview.banner">This case file walks through the two-part investigation first — the Bengaluru facility deep-dive, then a 13-branch Pan-India survey — before naming the fix. Start at Phase 1.</span></div>
      </div>


      <!-- PHASE 1 -->
      <div class="panel active" id="p-phase1">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow" data-ck="phase1.eyebrow">Phase 1</span>
          <h2 data-ck="phase1.heading">Bengaluru facility walkthrough</h2>
          <p class="desc" data-ck="phase1.intro">On instruction from senior management, the first step was a direct walkthrough of the Bengaluru warehouse to understand system-coordinator work end to end — before touching any data.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="timeline">
          <div class="tl-item">
            <span class="tl-tag" data-ck="phase1.step1.tag">Step 1</span>
            <h4 data-ck="phase1.step1.title">Warehouse walkthrough</h4>
            <p data-ck="phase1.step1.desc">Observed pickup, retrieval, secure destruction and archival activity on the floor, and shadowed how system coordinators actually spend their day.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-item">
            <span class="tl-tag" data-ck="phase1.step2.tag">Step 2</span>
            <h4 data-ck="phase1.step2.title">Auto-forward the inbox</h4>
            <p data-ck="phase1.step2.desc">Set up auto-forwarding of the branch's customer-facing mailboxes so incoming volume could be measured directly, instead of estimated.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-item">
            <span class="tl-tag" data-ck="phase1.step3.tag">Step 3</span>
            <h4 data-ck="phase1.step3.title">Measure one week of real traffic</h4>
            <p data-ck="phase1.step3.desc">Logged every incoming email for a full week and split it by request type.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-item">
            <span class="tl-tag" data-ck="phase1.step4.tag">Step 4</span>
            <h4 data-ck="phase1.step4.title">Read the pattern</h4>
            <p data-ck="phase1.step4.desc">Requests were arriving across email, Astra and phone calls with no shared tracking — so staff were spending more time answering "what's the status?" than doing the underlying work.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="chart-card" style="margin-top:26px;">
          <h3 data-ck="phase1.chartTitle">One week of Bengaluru email volume</h3>
          <p class="note" data-ck="phase1.chartNote">Counted directly from the auto-forwarded mailboxes.</p>
          <div class="chart-holder"><div class="svg-chart" id="chart-bengaluru"></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- PHASE 2 -->
      <div class="panel" id="p-phase2">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow" data-ck="phase2.eyebrow">Phase 2</span>
          <h2 data-ck="phase2.heading">Pan-India operations survey — 13 branches</h2>
          <p class="desc" data-ck="phase2.intro">Bengaluru already had the solution in hand (Astra), so the follow-up question was national: how are the other branches coping, and how far has Astra actually reached? A structured survey went out to 13 locations. The chart below excludes Bengaluru, which is covered separately in Phase 1.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="chart-card">
          <h3 data-ck="phase2.chartTitle">Daily request load by branch <span style="font-weight:400; color:var(--ink-soft); font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:11px;">(Bengaluru excluded)</span></h3>
          <p class="note" data-ck="phase2.chartNote">Self-reported by the branch operations lead. Ranges given in the survey were averaged for charting.</p>
          <div class="chart-legend">
            <span class="leg-item"><span class="leg-swatch" style="background:#194045;"></span>Daily emails</span>
            <span class="leg-item"><span class="leg-swatch" style="background:#b98a34;"></span>New requests / day</span>
            <span class="leg-item"><span class="leg-swatch" style="background:#a8432f;"></span>Follow-ups / day</span>
          </div>
          <div class="chart-holder scrolls"><div class="svg-chart" id="chart-panindia"></div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="folder">
          <span class="folder-tab" data-ck="phase2.findTab">What the survey surfaced</span>
          <div class="folder-body">
            <ul class="findings-list">
              <li><span class="n">·</span> <span data-ck="phase2.find1">Every branch listed email as a channel, and most also had Astra — but the split between them varies widely by branch.</span></li>
              <li><span class="n">·</span> <span data-ck="phase2.find2">Mumbai and Delhi carry the heaviest daily email load of the branches surveyed.</span></li>
              <li><span class="n">·</span> <span data-ck="phase2.find3">Recurring operational blockers: manpower shortage, storage/rack space, and inconsistent system access — echoing what Bengaluru showed on the floor.</span></li>
              <li><span class="n">·</span> <span data-ck="phase2.find4">Several branch leads independently flagged wanting to convert email-heavy customers into Astra users.</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ASTRA & FINDINGS -->
      <div class="panel" id="p-astra">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow" data-ck="astra.eyebrow">Findings</span>
          <h2 data-ck="astra.heading">Key Findings from the Operations Assessment</h2>
          <p class="desc" data-ck="astra.intro">Astra already handles pickup, retrieval, secure destruction and reporting, and is fully live in Singapore, Malaysia and the Philippines. The India gap is not a product gap — it's a rollout gap.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="chart-card">
          <h3 data-ck="astra.chartTitle">Astra adoption by market</h3>
          <p class="note" data-ck="astra.chartNote">Malaysia and the Philippines show what mandated rollout looks like once the enterprise adopts the tool.</p>
          <div class="chart-holder"><div class="svg-chart" id="chart-astra"></div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid-2" style="margin-top:22px;">
          <div class="folder" style="margin-top:0;">
            <span class="folder-tab" data-ck="astra.rootTab">Root Causes</span>
            <div class="folder-body">
              <ul class="findings-list">
                <li><span class="n">1</span> <span data-ck="astra.root1">Astra is being sold at the wrong level of the customer organization — to the people who use email daily, not the people who can mandate a tool.</span></li>
                <li><span class="n">2</span> <span data-ck="astra.root2">There is no single owner for Astra with both the IT and customer-relationship skillset the rollout needs.</span></li>
                <li><span class="n">3</span> <span data-ck="astra.root3">This is a B2B contract: the enterprise mandates the tool, and once mandated, users follow — as seen in Malaysia and the Philippines.</span></li>
                <li><span class="n">4</span> <span data-ck="astra.root4">Astra's governed, SSO-based access model is actually the stronger security story versus ungoverned email — it just isn't being told that way.</span></li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="folder" style="margin-top:0;">
            <span class="folder-tab" data-ck="astra.verdictTab">Verdict</span>
            <div class="folder-body">
              <p style="margin-bottom:10px;"><b style="color:var(--teal-950);" data-ck="astra.verdictLabel">Identified as a rollout failure</b>, not a product failure.</p>
              <p data-ck="astra.verdictText">No one has pitched Astra to the people who can mandate it, and no one owns the end-to-end rollout with both the IT and the customer-relationship skillset it needs.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="quote-block" style="margin-top:22px;">
          "<span data-ck="astra.quote">Astra is the interface to RSSQL for our customers — but to the customer, they don't care whether it's RSSQL or Astra, they just want something with an easy user interface that provides whatever reports or information to them. That's where the differentiator is in terms of how an Iron Mountain person would present RS Web compared to how Crown presents Astra.</span>"
          <cite data-ck="astra.quoteCite">— Stakeholder interview, Pan-India assessment</cite>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- INCENTIVE PLAN -->
      <div class="panel" id="p-incentive">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow" data-ck="incentive.eyebrow">Incentive Plan — Additional Ideas</span>
          <h2 data-ck="incentive.heading">Structured incentives to accelerate adoption</h2>
          <p class="desc" data-ck="incentive.intro">Suggested mechanics, informed by how B2B loyalty programs drive retention and referrals in practice.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="incentive-grid">
          <div class="incentive-card">
            <h4 data-ck="incentive.card1.title">Migration credit</h4>
            <p data-ck="incentive.card1.desc">A one-time service credit (e.g. waived charges on the next retrieval or destruction order) for any legacy account that completes its move to Astra within a defined window.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="incentive-card">
            <h4 data-ck="incentive.card2.title">Volume-linked pricing tiers</h4>
            <p data-ck="incentive.card2.desc">Preferential per-transaction rates for accounts once they cross an Astra-usage threshold — rewarding usage, not just tenure, so it directly reinforces the behaviour we want.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="incentive-card">
            <h4 data-ck="incentive.card3.title">"Champion within the bank" recognition</h4>
            <p data-ck="incentive.card3.desc">A named point of contact inside each client bank who drives Astra usage internally gets recognized directly — addressing that the real decision-maker is rarely the one who benefits today.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="incentive-card">
            <h4 data-ck="incentive.card4.title">Early-access &amp; co-development seat</h4>
            <p data-ck="incentive.card4.desc">Top-tenure accounts get a seat in a quarterly product-feedback session, with priority visibility into fixes like maker-checker and reporting enhancements.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="incentive-card">
            <h4 data-ck="incentive.card5.title">Referral incentive</h4>
            <p data-ck="incentive.card5.desc">A structured discount or service credit when an existing loyal account refers another bank or branch network that signs on to Astra.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="incentive-card">
            <h4 data-ck="incentive.card6.title">Annual loyalty review</h4>
            <p data-ck="incentive.card6.desc">A yearly account review that explicitly states tenure, savings generated via Astra automation, and SLA performance — making the relationship's value visible, not assumed.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- AUTOMATION ROADMAP -->
      <div class="panel" id="p-roadmap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow" data-ck="roadmap.eyebrow">For customers resistant to change</span>
          <h2 data-ck="roadmap.heading">An automation fallback, for accounts that won't move off email</h2>
          <p class="desc" data-ck="roadmap.intro">Where a customer relationship simply won't shift to Astra in the near term, the process itself can still be automated so the branch stops paying the "what's the status" tax.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="flow">
          <div class="fbox"><b data-ck="roadmap.flow1.label">Step 1</b><span data-ck="roadmap.flow1.desc">One inbox, Pan-India — a single consolidated address instead of scattered branch mailboxes.</span></div>
          <div class="arrow">→</div>
          <div class="fbox"><b data-ck="roadmap.flow2.label">Step 2</b><span data-ck="roadmap.flow2.desc">Auto-classify on arrival — every incoming email is tagged by request type automatically.</span></div>
          <div class="arrow">→</div>
          <div class="fbox branch-yes"><b data-ck="roadmap.flow3.label">If service request</b><span data-ck="roadmap.flow3.desc">Auto-redirected straight to the right team queue.</span></div>
          <div class="arrow">/</div>
          <div class="fbox branch-no"><b data-ck="roadmap.flow4.label">If not a service request</b><span data-ck="roadmap.flow4.desc">Auto-ticketed, so it's tracked instead of silently sitting in an inbox.</span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="folder">
          <span class="folder-tab" data-ck="roadmap.whyTab">Why this matters even with Astra live</span>
          <div class="folder-body">
            <p data-ck="roadmap.whyText">The rollout plan above should close most of the gap over time — but some accounts will resist change regardless of pitch quality. This fallback gives every request a shared source of status, even for customers still on email, closing the exact visibility gap the Bengaluru walkthrough surfaced.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- DOWNLOAD REPORT -->
      <div class="panel" id="p-report">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow" data-ck="report.eyebrow">Source Document</span>
          <h2 data-ck="report.heading">Operational Assessment Report</h2>
          <p class="desc" data-ck="report.intro">The full write-up behind this dashboard — stakeholder discussions and process-walkthrough observations from the Bengaluru assessment.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="download-panel">
          <div>
            <h3 data-ck="report.fileTitle">Operational_Assessment_Report.pdf</h3>
            <p data-ck="report.fileDesc">Customer service &amp; retrieval process findings, prepared from stakeholder discussions and process walkthrough observations.</p>
          </div>
          <button class="btn btn-gold" id="btn-download-report">⬇ Download PDF</button>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
    <footer class="sign" data-ck="footer.text">Prepared during internship placement · Customer Service Operations Project</footer>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== USER DASHBOARD — PROJECT TWO ===================== -->
  <section id="view-dashboard-p2" class="screen hidden">
    <div class="topbar">
      <div class="brand">
        <div class="mark">CR</div>
        <div class="brand-text">
          <div class="name">Project Two · Enterprise Prospect Strategy</div>
          <div class="role">Customer Relationship · Internship Project</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="who">
        <button class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" id="btn-projects-p2">← All Projects</button>
        <span class="who-name">Signed in as <b id="dash-who-name-p2">—</b></span>
        <button class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" id="btn-logout-p2">Log out</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tabs" id="p2-tabs">
      <button class="tab-btn active" data-panel="p2-research">Research Methodology</button>
      <button class="tab-btn" data-panel="p2-market">What the Data Shows</button>
      <button class="tab-btn" data-panel="p2-recs">Strategic Recommendations</button>
      <button class="tab-btn" data-panel="p2-services">Service Portfolio</button>
      <button class="tab-btn" data-panel="p2-report">Download Report</button>
    </div>

    <div class="content-wrap">
      <div class="banner">
        <div class="banner-text"><b>Note:</b> This case file digs through the research first — industry, compliance, digital maturity, financials — before naming a single service. Start at Research Methodology.</div>
      </div>

      <!-- RESEARCH METHODOLOGY -->
      <div class="panel active" id="p2-research">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">Phase 1 · Research</span>
          <h2>Profiling the prospect before profiling the pitch</h2>
          <p class="desc">Before any service was proposed, every prospect was run through the same multi-tiered analytical framework — not just financial capacity, but operational risk and technological readiness. The goal was to understand each organisation on the ground, the same way Project One started with a facility walkthrough rather than a sales deck.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="timeline">
          <div class="tl-item">
            <span class="tl-tag">Step 1</span>
            <h4>Industry categorisation &amp; PESTEL scoring</h4>
            <p>Each of the 38 organisations was mapped to its core industry, then scored on a customised Political / Economic / Social / Technological / Environmental / Legal scorecard to establish a priority rank and gauge how receptive the business is likely to be to change.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-item">
            <span class="tl-tag">Step 2</span>
            <h4>Compliance level &amp; digital maturity</h4>
            <p>Regulatory burden was assessed by industry (e.g. RBI guidance for banks, FDA-style rules for pharma), alongside whether the organisation is paper-heavy, mid-transition, or fully digitised — informed by its current ERP, CRM and document-management adoption.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-item">
            <span class="tl-tag">Step 3</span>
            <h4>Operational &amp; financial data</h4>
            <p>Revenue, EBIT, capital expenditure, fixed-asset additions and asset-to-profit ratio were pulled from corporate filings to gauge scale and where a fixed-asset or document solution would actually move the needle.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-item">
            <span class="tl-tag">Step 4</span>
            <h4>Footprint &amp; SEZ status</h4>
            <p>India footprint, headcount, and — critically — Special Economic Zone status were mapped. SEZ operations carry heavier audit and paperwork burdens, which flags them early as candidates for tighter tracking.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="folder">
          <span class="folder-tab">Why this order</span>
          <div class="folder-body">
            <p>Every one of these steps is diagnostic, not promotional — the same discipline as Project One's facility walkthrough before touching any data. The service catalogue only shows up once the diagnosis is complete, in the last tab of this case file.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- MARKET INSIGHTS -->
      <div class="panel" id="p2-market">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">Phase 2 · What the data shows</span>
          <h2>38 prospects, one recurring blind spot</h2>
          <p class="desc">Aggregating the research phase across all 38 evaluated organisations surfaces a technology-adoption pattern — and one adoption number that stands out for being so much lower than the rest.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid-3" style="margin-bottom:26px;">
          <div class="index-card"><span class="num">38</span><span class="label">Enterprise prospects evaluated</span></div>
          <div class="index-card"><span class="num">₹19,120 Cr</span><span class="label">Average top-line revenue across the base</span></div>
          <div class="index-card"><span class="num">81.6%</span><span class="label">Already running an ERP system</span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="chart-card" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
          <h3>Industry concentration</h3>
          <p class="note">Where the 38 evaluated prospects sit, by primary sector.</p>
          <div class="chart-holder"><div class="svg-chart" id="chart-industry"></div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="chart-card">
          <h3>Technology use — where the biggest gap is</h3>
          <p class="note">ERP and document-management systems are widely used. Customer-management systems are much less common.</p>
          <div class="chart-holder"><div class="svg-chart" id="chart-techadopt"></div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="folder">
          <span class="folder-tab">What the survey surfaced</span>
          <div class="folder-body">
            <ul class="findings-list">
              <li><span class="n">·</span> <span>Banking &amp; Financial Services, Food/Beverage/Tobacco manufacturing, and Hospital &amp; Health Services carry the heaviest regulatory load and the densest physical-asset footprints.</span></li>
              <li><span class="n">·</span> <span>78.9% of prospects already run some form of document-management system — but the qualitative review found most of those setups lack AI-driven OCR or workflow automation.</span></li>
              <li><span class="n">·</span> <span>Only 13.2% of the 38 prospects use a customer-management system (CRM) — the largest technology gap identified in the study.</span></li>
              <li><span class="n">·</span> <span>22 of the 38 prospects have Special Economic Zone operations, meaning they face disproportionate compliance and audit-documentation burden.</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="folder">
          <span class="folder-tab">Challenges &amp; Data Limitations</span>
          <div class="folder-body"><ul class="findings-list">
            <li><span class="n">1</span> <span>Obtaining accurate details on the DMS, CRM and ERP systems used by every customer was difficult because this information is not consistently available.</span></li>
            <li><span class="n">2</span> <span>The Bengaluru customer analysis faced accuracy limitations because of the large customer volume and limited reliable customer-level system information.</span></li>
            <li><span class="n">3</span> <span>Only a subset of the available customer data could be analysed because of limited resources and incomplete data availability.</span></li>
            <li><span class="n">4</span> <span>The results should therefore be treated as a research-based opportunity assessment rather than a complete technology inventory for every customer.</span></li>
          </ul></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- STRATEGIC RECOMMENDATIONS -->
      <div class="panel" id="p2-recs">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">Diagnosis</span>
          <h2>Four data-backed plays — not a product pitch</h2>
          <p class="desc">Cross-referencing financial health, digital maturity and PESTEL pressure against the survey above points to a deployment sequence, not a single blanket offer.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="folder" style="margin-top:0;">
          <span class="folder-tab">Recommended sequence</span>
          <div class="folder-body">
            <ul class="findings-list">
              <li><span class="n">1</span> <span>Prioritise SEZ-registered entities first — they must track assets strictly to justify tax benefits and satisfy government audits, so a bundled documentation-and-asset-tracking offer lands with the least persuasion needed.</span></li>
              <li><span class="n">2</span> <span>Target high-Capex prospects for fixed-asset tracking — entities with large capital expenditure and fixed-asset additions get the clearest, fastest-to-prove return from better lifecycle tracking and reduced loss.</span></li>
              <li><span class="n">3</span> <span>Upsell the 78.9% already on some document system — the pitch shifts from "go digital" to "make your existing system actually work for you," which is a very different, much easier conversation.</span></li>
              <li><span class="n">4</span> <span>Use compliance risk as the opener for regulated and software-dependent prospects — physical-file retrieval delays and vendor-continuity risk are framed as exposure being carried today, not a future nice-to-have.</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="quote-block" style="margin-top:22px;">
          This project is a shift from broad-spectrum sales to precision-targeted outreach. Ranking prospects by PESTEL pressure, compliance load and financial scale — before choosing what to offer — turns each proposed service into an answer to a problem the prospect already has, rather than a feature list looking for a buyer.
          <cite>— Strategic Prospect Analysis, closing summary</cite>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- SERVICE PORTFOLIO (the solution — last) -->
      <div class="panel" id="p2-services">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">The Toolkit — arriving last, on purpose</span>
          <h2>Once the diagnosis is clear, here's what actually closes the gap</h2>
          <p class="desc">Every service below exists to answer something the research surfaced — not the other way round. The CRM gap identified in Market Insights is the throughline: it's what makes the customer <i>relationship</i>, not just the transaction, the thing being sold.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="incentive-grid">
          <div class="incentive-card">
            <h4>EffiDocs (Document Management)</h4>
            <p>Lite, Plus and Pro tiers matched to digital maturity — Pro adds an AI engine for auto-extracting data fields and generating documents, aimed squarely at the 78.9% already on a DMS who are ready to upgrade.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="incentive-card">
            <h4>DART (Dispatch · Ack. · Reconciliation · Tracking)</h4>
            <p>Secures the physical lifecycle of critical files across branches and storage, with real-time turnaround monitoring for regulated entities that can't afford delayed document retrieval.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="incentive-card">
            <h4>FAMS (Fixed Asset Management)</h4>
            <p>QR/RFID-based asset tracking from procurement to disposal — built for the high-Capex prospects flagged in the recommendations, directly improving the asset-to-profit ratio.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="incentive-card">
            <h4>Visio (Visitor Management)</h4>
            <p>Replaces paper logbooks with digitised, pre-registered check-ins and mandatory digital NDAs — including a single-credential module for long-term contract staff like external auditors.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="incentive-card">
            <h4>Source Code Escrow</h4>
            <p>A neutral third party holds a vendor's source code, releasing it to the client if the vendor fails — business-continuity protection for software-dependent and BFSI cloud relationships.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="incentive-card">
            <h4>Why this closes the CRM gap</h4>
            <p>None of these tools is a CRM replacement — but together they give the account team a reason to be in regular, structured contact with each prospect, which is the relationship layer that was missing.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="chart-card" style="margin-top:24px;">
          <h3>Where each service is already being recommended</h3>
          <p class="note">Number of the 38 evaluated prospects for which each service was flagged as a fit.</p>
          <div class="chart-holder"><div class="svg-chart" id="chart-services"></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- DOWNLOAD REPORT -->
      <div class="panel" id="p2-report">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">Source Documents</span>
          <h2>Strategic Prospect Analysis &amp; Service Alignment</h2>
          <p class="desc">The full write-up and the underlying prospect-level workbook behind this dashboard.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="download-panel" style="margin-bottom:16px;">
          <div><h3>Project Two Report</h3><p>Download the research methodology, market insights, challenges, recommendations and service alignment shown in this case file.</p></div>
          <button class="btn btn-gold" id="btn-download-p2-report">⬇ Download Report</button>
        </div>
        <div class="download-panel"><div><h3>Source Documents</h3><p>The dashboard references the prospect workbook and supporting project report. Additional original files can be added to the Admin Report Library when supplied.</p>
          <div style="margin-top:16px;display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
            <a class="btn btn-ghost" id="btn-download-p2-source-xlsx" href="data:application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet;base64," download="Enriched_Main_Updated.xlsx">⬇ Download Source Spreadsheet</a>
          </div>
        </div><span class="stamp" style="transform:rotate(0deg);">Source document-managed</span></div>
      </div>

    </div>
